cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Lane-Change-MCU: lane-change prediction on STM32 microcontrollers with searched
  and hand-designed 1D CNNs
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sepehr
    family-names: Mohammady
    affiliation: >-
      ELIOS Lab, Department of Electrical, Electronic and Telecommunications
      Engineering and Naval Architecture (DITEN), University of Genoa, Italy
repository-code: https://github.com/SepehrMohammady/Lane-Change-MCU
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Searched (muNAS) and hand-designed 1D CNNs for driver intention (LCIR) and
  surrounding-vehicle lane changes (highD and exiD), retrained with five
  seeds and deployed to Arm Cortex-M7 and Cortex-M4 microcontrollers with
  measured latency, flash and RAM from the ST Edge AI board farm.
keywords:
  - neural architecture search
  - TinyML
  - lane change prediction
  - time to lane change
  - quantization
  - STM32
  - embedded machine learning
  - intelligent transportation systems
